  "prefLabel": "Ins 207.08 Record Retention",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 207.08 Record Retention. The department shall keep a decision or order on file in its records for at least 6 years following the date of the final decision or the date of the decision on any appeal, unless the director of the division of records management and archives of the department of state sets a different retention period pursuant to rules adopted under RSA 541:31.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
